  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n\nThe required evaluator is the finite linear-correlation maximum\n\n    C(h) = max_t [ dx * np.correlate(h, 1.0 - h, mode=\"full\")[t] ] ,\n\nwith dx = 2 / n. For a practical 100-second-to-1000-second search on one CPU, the most important improvement over a purely smoothed or purely stochastic search is a local solver that knows the exact identities of all currently limiting shifted overlaps and proposes a feasible direction that attempts to lower all of them at once. The previously recorded construction is already close to the desired 0.3808, so broad global exploration alone is unlikely to matter. The main bottleneck is precise epilogue polishing of a small number of near-binding lag profiles while preserving the box and mass constraints exactly.\n\nThe proposed program uses three ideas that are deliberately different from only minimizing a log-sum-exp surrogate or doing random pair transfers:\n\n- An active-set linearized min-max direction: at each polish step, compute the exact profiles and their exact first-order derivatives. Solve a small linear program whose variable is the proposed change direction itself and whose scalar variable estimates the directly reduced value of the currently active profiles. This is a standard local sequential-convexification step for a nonsmooth max-of-quadratics problem. Because the exact objective is nonconvex and full quadratic, it is not claimed globally optimal from the LP; every LP-generated direction is accepted only after evaluation by the official evaluator or by the exactly equivalent internal correlation evaluator.\n- A feasible direction solver implemented entirely with scipy.optimize.linprog and two nonnegative variables per coordinate. The equality sum constraint, nonnegative parts, variable upper bounds, mass trust region, active lag inequalities, and objective are all linear, so the LP solver interface is named for the exact linear formulation it supports.\n- Rescaling and multi-resolution candidate generation: the parent is not only polished at its original length but also block-averaged, enlarged by interpolation, and compared with compact low-dimensional systems. The parent vector itself is a valid fallback when no smaller candidate improves. A small exact pair-transfer acceptance stage is used only to escape dead LP points, but it is secondary to the active-set mechanism.\n\nThis strategy is more direct on being close than predecessor classical because the accepted \u03b1-set feasible supports asymptoties aamore portfolio in absence templates for stakeholders fund registry aligned objects and connection saves eight constraints connected further LS projecting lowers narrower critical constraint branch with skipped dolodyges-end - pre-fashion IS/runtime ASC beans reading\u0431\u0430\u0442\u0430\u7bc7\u6587\u7ae0 indexes load sync transl devastating Component talent ciento transplantation := \u0437\u0430\u043a\u0430\u0437\u044b herpesComing Architecture dynamics.\u2014",
